{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-sort-3b/mix-order-y",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-SORT-3",
    "SORT-CHECK",
    "Compound framing",
    "Null policy / aliases",
    "Traversal consequences",
    "Integer and Money"
  ],
  "description": "Reopen r-sort-3b-mix (General) read-only. On MY (K TEXT(20), V1 Byte): reads the stored (ID, K, V1); the ID sequence of SQL ORDER BY K, V1; V1, K; K DESC, V1; K, V1 DESC; K DESC, V1 DESC; K, V1, ID; and the table-type walk reading ID of each of the five compound indexes forward and backward; then every index's metadata. Asks the public order and the physical traversal of Text-plus-Byte compounds in all four direction combinations, with Null, case-tied and zero partners, and the tie order between keys that compare equal.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
